<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Deliberately empty.

  The Hardened Runtime that notarisation requires is a set of restrictions, and
  an entitlement here is a hole punched back through one of them. Ocarina needs
  none of the usual ones: it renders its own window with ImageRenderer rather
  than capturing the screen, and forkpty/execve are untouched by the Hardened
  Runtime — the shell it launches is signed by Apple and validated on its own
  terms, not the parent's.

  Two that a change to the app could make necessary, and nothing else without a
  failure to point at first:

    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
      only if a dylib that is not signed by this team has to load in-process.
    com.apple.security.automation.apple-events
      only if the app starts driving another one over AppleEvents.

  The file is still passed to codesign while empty, so that adding an
  entitlement is an edit here rather than a change to how the app is signed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
